<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="47810" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/BIOE/199/47810.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="BIOE" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/BIOE.xml">Bioengineering</subject><course id="199" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/BIOE/199.xml">Undergraduate Open Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>CHP</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Bioengineering Experience</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Bioengineering is a multidisciplinary field that utilizes engineering tools and principles to solve issues related to medicine and human health. In this course, students will be exposed to a variety of sub-topics that encompass the diverse field of bioengineering through a multitude of experiences, including lectures, guest seminars, lab tours, hands-on activities and demonstrations, team-based biomedical design challenges, and basic laboratory experiments that demonstrate the scientific process. This course is open to Campus Honors Students only.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>02:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MWF    </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>0018</roomNumber><buildingName>Campus Instructional Facility</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Cvetkovic" firstName="C">Cvetkovic, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>